@Kate, You can achieve what you want by adding a CSS rule in one of your theme's CSS files. For example, if you are using the afterburner theme, add the new rule at the end of theme/afterburner/style/afterburner_layout.css . example #1: to display links vertically, as a bullet-list: 
```text
#page-mod-lesson-view .lessonbutton {display:list-item; text-align:left; margin-left:15px;}
```
 example #2: to space out horizontal links: 
```text
#page-mod-lesson-view .lessonbutton {margin-right:20px;}
```
 See attached screenshots - using afterburner. Please copy-paste or write exactly as in my examples the CSS rules. I have not checked if these rules might have side-effects in displaying other parts of the Lesson activity, so use at own risk. Hope that helps, Joseph

